      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "How can we best describe the following matrix?\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nChoose the most specific listed description: identity before diagonal, and diagonal before upper or lower triangular. Choose Other only if none of these descriptions applies.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries above the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, it is a lower triangular matrix.\n\nIt is not an upper triangular matrix or a diagonal matrix since there is a non-zero element below the diagonal: ${a}_{21}=6\\ne 0.$",
